<div class="case__block">
  <h3>The brief</h3>
  <p>
    Banning Glass Mirror and Screen do glass, mirror and screen work for people around Banning
    &mdash; the kind of business where most of the work has always come through word of mouth
    and the phone. What they needed was somewhere for that word of mouth to land: a place a
    customer could actually find when someone passed their name along, or when a search for a
    local glass company turned up nothing useful.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not a brochure. Something that told people what they do, made it obvious how to reach them,
    and did not get in the way on a phone.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="case__block">
  <h3>What I did</h3>
  <p>
    I built the site by hand rather than starting from a template, because a bought theme would
    have meant bending their business to fit somebody else&rsquo;s layout. The structure follows
    the work they actually take on, in their own words, and every page keeps the phone number in
    reach &mdash; on a phone it is one tap.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is built to be quick. Most people looking for a glass company are standing in front of
    the broken thing, on a phone, with whatever signal they have. A site that takes five seconds
    to load has already lost that call.
  </p>
